## Purpose

Turn App Server and Work Efficiency observations into truthful, bounded operational trends and
view-faithful exports without retaining heartbeat noise or implying unsupported comparisons.

## Desired Outcome

An operator can select a bounded window, see what changed with its coverage and epoch context, and
export exactly the allowlisted filtered rows shown on screen with explicit schema and row limits.

## First Useful Boundary

- Retain change-only Work Efficiency observations with a bounded server-side retention limit.
- Present a compact trend table for a small set of useful windows with freshness, sample count,
  platform/version, coverage, and reset/epoch qualifications.
- Add CSV and JSON export of the same active filtered projection, schema-versioned and capped.
- Preserve explicit unknown and incomparable states; avoid smoothing, ranking, and causal claims.
- Qualify deduplication, retention, filtering, export privacy, response cost, and live rendering,
  then deploy through Work2.

## Workstreams

| Workstream | Outcome | Depends On |
| --- | --- | --- |
| History contract | Change-only semantic observations with retention and epoch boundaries | accepted reports |
| Trend projection | Bounded windows with coverage and comparison qualifications | history contract |
| Export surface | View-faithful capped CSV/JSON projection | trend projection |
| Qualification | Deduplication, retention, privacy, filtering, rendering, deployment, and browser evidence | complete vertical slice |

## Readiness Gate Transfer

1. `G1-CHANGE-ONLY-TREND-HISTORY` requires semantic-change retention, duplicate suppression,
   counter epochs, freshness, and a bounded retention policy.
2. `G2-TRUTHFUL-TREND-SEMANTICS` requires coverage, sample windows, reset boundaries, and explicit
   unknown or incomparable states.
3. `G3-BOUNDED-VIEW-EXPORT` limits exports to the active allowlisted projection with schema,
   generation time, and row cap.

## Constraints

- Reuse accepted report and Work Efficiency models; do not retain raw heartbeat events.
- Partial token coverage and different epochs, platforms, or versions are visibly qualified.
- Export never includes prompts, source, paths, commands, raw failures, credentials, or local DB rows.

## Non-Goals

- A business-intelligence platform, arbitrary query builder, or public analytics API.
- Project rankings, release causality claims, or automatic comparison across incompatible cohorts.

